WEBVTT

00:03:14.560 --> 00:03:17.080
How are you, sir? How are you, Caterine?

00:03:17.890 --> 00:03:19.920
Come with me.

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:22.720
Come with me.

00:03:23.090 --> 00:03:24.070
It's a beautiful thing.

00:03:24.710 --> 00:03:28.040
We found something wonderful.

00:03:28.500 --> 00:03:29.580
A great surprise.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:31.660
I can't believe it.

00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:32.620
What a surprise.

00:03:33.460 --> 00:03:35.600
Come on, come on.

00:03:37.060 --> 00:03:39.220
Look, look.

00:03:39.340 --> 00:03:41.290
Look here, look.

00:03:41.410 --> 00:03:42.670
What a beautiful thing.

00:03:42.870 --> 00:03:51.310
What do we have here?

00:03:53.910 --> 00:03:54.470
Covering stones.

00:03:54.930 --> 00:03:55.490
Fantastic.

00:04:05.370 --> 00:04:06.270
Catherine, come here!

00:04:07.420 --> 00:04:09.350
Look! Look what we found!

00:04:09.750 --> 00:04:14.190
Be careful with the rope!

00:04:50.760 --> 00:04:52.320
In the name of jutsu, what is this?

00:04:52.980 --> 00:04:53.780
I'd like to know.

00:05:14.490 --> 00:05:24.400
There are symbols painted everywhere. Names, property titles, offerings lists, and other great architectural structures of the time were covered with detailed hieroglyphs.

00:05:24.500 --> 00:05:29.980
When will the academic community accept the fact that the pharaohs of the fourth dynasty did not build...

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:31.260
They built the Great Pyramids.

00:05:31.360 --> 00:05:35.280
Listen, listen, inside the pyramid,

00:05:35.460 --> 00:05:37.960
the most amazing structure ever built,

00:05:38.160 --> 00:05:40.240
believe me, there is no writing.

00:05:41.080 --> 00:05:44.980
Dr. Jackson, forget the fact that Colonel Weiss

00:05:44.980 --> 00:05:47.820
discovered inscriptions of workers in stone walls

00:05:47.820 --> 00:05:51.500
with the name of Khufu inside the pyramid.

00:05:51.860 --> 00:05:53.160
The discovery is a fact.

00:05:53.320 --> 00:05:54.480
Well, I hope I can prove it.

00:05:56.350 --> 00:05:58.150
Well, who do you think built the pyramids?

00:06:03.100 --> 00:06:05.520
I have no idea who built them, I'm just saying...

00:06:05.520 --> 00:06:07.800
Atlantean men? Or maybe Marcians?

00:06:08.720 --> 00:06:12.540
The question is not who built them, but when they were built.

00:06:12.980 --> 00:06:19.780
We all know the new geological evidence that the Sphinx dates from a much earlier period.

00:06:19.960 --> 00:06:25.520
Knowing this, I think we should re-evaluate everything we believe about this time, and I...

00:06:25.520 --> 00:06:27.520
This is ridiculous, I think I've wasted my time.

00:06:27.520 --> 00:06:29.500
I was able to show a system of total...

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:33.640
developed, emerged in the first two dynasties.

00:06:33.680 --> 00:06:38.650
You know, as if it were based on an even older prototype.

00:06:38.770 --> 00:06:43.230
Hey, what is it, lunch time?

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:00.440
Dr. Jekyll!

00:07:00.540 --> 00:07:01.770
Me? Why?

00:07:02.260 --> 00:07:03.540
Someone wants to talk to you.

00:07:03.800 --> 00:07:06.480
The Air Force? Why?

00:07:06.900 --> 00:07:09.510
Could you go to the car, please, sir?

00:07:13.020 --> 00:07:13.240
Sir?

00:07:13.460 --> 00:07:18.860
Are we going somewhere?

00:07:19.300 --> 00:07:21.360
Don't worry, sir. We'll take care of it.

00:07:28.280 --> 00:07:29.790
Daniel, be careful.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:40.100
He's already dead. What does all this mean?

00:07:40.410 --> 00:07:40.810
Work.

00:07:42.340 --> 00:07:43.540
What kind of work?

00:07:44.140 --> 00:07:47.120
Translation. Ancient Egyptian hieroglyphs.

00:07:51.400 --> 00:07:52.000
Interested?

00:07:54.900 --> 00:07:55.700
I'm leaving.

00:07:56.920 --> 00:07:57.240
Where to?

00:07:58.520 --> 00:07:59.960
You've just been evicted.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:02.420
Your apartment is empty. Your money is gone.

00:08:03.510 --> 00:08:05.530
Everything you own is in these two bags.

00:08:05.890 --> 00:08:09.780
Do you want to prove that your theories are true?

00:08:12.120 --> 00:08:13.020
It's your chance.

00:08:17.210 --> 00:08:17.830
What's that?

00:08:18.410 --> 00:08:19.290
Travel plans.

00:08:19.630 --> 00:08:19.830
Sir!

00:09:07.480 --> 00:09:08.900
Is your husband at home, Mrs. O'Neill?

00:09:09.000 --> 00:09:09.180
Yes.

00:09:10.600 --> 00:09:13.620
Do you think we can talk to him?

00:09:15.840 --> 00:09:16.300
You can try.

00:09:18.160 --> 00:09:18.900
Tyler O'Neill.

00:09:19.460 --> 00:09:20.420
Liga Mirim Sportivity Award.

00:09:50.730 --> 00:09:54.360
Excuse me, Colonel O'Neill. We are from the office of General West, sir.

00:10:02.720 --> 00:10:05.340
We came to inform you that you are back active.

00:10:05.600 --> 00:10:17.550
The guy is finished. How did he get like this?

00:10:17.730 --> 00:10:21.620
The son died in an accident with a weapon.

00:10:22.150 --> 00:10:22.470
Wow!

00:10:32.970 --> 00:10:34.010
Military installation.

00:10:34.570 --> 00:10:35.550
Forbidden entry.

00:10:56.180 --> 00:10:56.860
Allergy.

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:00.920
It's great when I travel.

00:11:01.140 --> 00:11:02.260
We're here.

00:11:04.220 --> 00:11:04.540
Hi.

00:11:06.860 --> 00:11:08.350
Dr. Jackson.

00:11:08.570 --> 00:11:09.800
Dr. Gary Myers.

00:11:09.940 --> 00:11:10.360
How are you?

00:11:10.460 --> 00:11:11.980
What is this place?

00:11:13.120 --> 00:11:13.600
Missile deposit.

00:11:13.600 --> 00:11:14.200
Don't worry.

00:11:14.420 --> 00:11:15.120
It was completely converted.

00:11:15.460 --> 00:11:16.040
Barbara Shore.

00:11:16.300 --> 00:11:16.600
Hi.

00:11:17.040 --> 00:11:17.520
Laboratory.

00:11:18.450 --> 00:11:18.930
Restricted access.

00:11:36.200 --> 00:11:39.100
Right, Daniel. Welcome to the well.

00:11:39.220 --> 00:11:43.760
Oh, hi. Where did you find that?

00:11:44.500 --> 00:11:46.660
Plateau de Guise, 1928.

00:11:48.140 --> 00:11:49.620
I've never seen anything like it.

00:11:49.800 --> 00:11:53.500
Of course not. No one's seen it.

00:11:53.670 --> 00:11:55.870
Well, there are two lines of hieroglyphs.

00:11:56.090 --> 00:11:58.130
Well, the inner trail has classic figures,

00:11:58.130 --> 00:11:59.670
but the outer one is like the...

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:02.740
there in the center. There are writings of the kind we've never seen before.

00:12:04.300 --> 00:12:07.100
They're not hieroglyphs. It must be some kind of erratic

00:12:07.100 --> 00:12:08.400
or maybe cuneiform.

00:12:09.750 --> 00:12:15.300
The translation of the inner trail is wrong. They must have used

00:12:15.300 --> 00:12:17.540
Bud. I don't know why they keep editing his books.

00:12:18.740 --> 00:12:21.960
Excuse me, but what are you doing? We've already used

00:12:21.960 --> 00:12:24.720
all the well-known techniques. It's a curious word for you to use,

00:12:24.840 --> 00:12:28.140
Geber. Is it? Then the adverb said enough,

00:12:28.760 --> 00:12:29.200
so...

00:12:31.040 --> 00:12:32.500
Sealed and buried.

00:12:32.540 --> 00:12:34.140
I'm sorry, what are you doing?

00:12:34.640 --> 00:12:35.960
This is not a coffin.

00:12:36.520 --> 00:12:37.380
It's forever.

00:12:39.330 --> 00:12:43.600
Who translated this?

00:12:45.890 --> 00:12:47.190
It was me. Why?

00:12:47.680 --> 00:12:48.520
Well, this says,

00:12:48.960 --> 00:12:50.440
A million years ago, in the sky,

00:12:50.600 --> 00:12:52.420
Ra, the god of the sun, sealed and buried,

00:12:53.960 --> 00:12:54.400
forever...

00:12:54.400 --> 00:12:55.900
No, it's not a door to heaven, it's...

00:13:02.460 --> 00:13:04.420
Stargate, or the portal of the stars.

00:13:05.450 --> 00:13:10.660
And why are the military so interested in 5,000-year-old Egyptian pieces?

00:13:10.720 --> 00:13:12.580
My report says 10,000.

00:13:14.020 --> 00:13:14.780
Good afternoon, Colonel.

00:13:20.910 --> 00:13:22.820
Uh, I know you.

00:13:23.390 --> 00:13:26.090
I'm Colonel Jack O'Neill, from the West's team.

00:13:26.090 --> 00:13:27.050
I'll take over from now on.

00:13:28.530 --> 00:13:29.980
This conversation...

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:33.120
10,000 years is an illusion. Egyptian culture didn't exist until...

00:13:33.120 --> 00:13:37.020
We know, but the radiocarbonic and sonic tests are conclusive.

00:13:37.360 --> 00:13:39.420
They're covered stones. There was a tomb under them.

00:13:39.520 --> 00:13:43.140
No, no, no. But we found something much, much more interesting.

00:13:43.440 --> 00:13:46.960
Excuse me. This information has become confidential.

00:13:48.920 --> 00:13:54.000
From now on, no information will be passed to non-military without my express permission.

00:13:58.140 --> 00:13:59.760
Katherine, what's going on?

00:14:00.700 --> 00:14:01.240
I don't know.

00:14:05.330 --> 00:14:08.560
Colonel Neo, I think you owe me an explanation.

00:14:09.900 --> 00:14:12.460
They told me that I would have total autonomy.

00:14:13.460 --> 00:14:14.160
Plans change.

00:14:15.380 --> 00:14:18.320
Why are you here? Why did you send me to this project?

00:14:22.000 --> 00:14:23.580
I'm here for the sake of success.

00:14:31.210 --> 00:14:34.790
Completed the search for hieroglyphs, cuneiforms and other pre-dynasties.

00:14:34.950 --> 00:14:35.750
No resemblance.

00:14:35.970 --> 00:14:39.990
I erased all the material references in the comparison of the symbols of the cartula

00:14:39.990 --> 00:14:42.970
with all the samples of writing of the pre- and post-period.

00:14:43.190 --> 00:14:47.390
No similarity. I will never receive.

00:15:15.000 --> 00:15:15.700
The Universe Today.

00:15:18.120 --> 00:15:18.960
Vista de Órion.

00:15:19.040 --> 00:15:24.460
Can I borrow it?

00:16:27.610 --> 00:16:28.090
Sit here.

00:16:28.230 --> 00:16:28.550
Okay.

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:31.020
I'd like to introduce you to General West.

00:16:31.320 --> 00:16:33.390
Oh, hi. Hi, hi, General.

00:16:34.430 --> 00:16:35.210
Hi. Cool.

00:16:37.250 --> 00:16:39.530
So you think you solved in 14 days

00:16:39.530 --> 00:16:41.610
what you couldn't solve in two years?

00:16:41.890 --> 00:16:43.510
Two years?

00:16:48.280 --> 00:16:48.900
Whenever you want.

00:16:50.870 --> 00:16:55.230
Uh, I have some things to show you.

00:16:55.250 --> 00:16:57.040
Uh, if I can go through.

00:16:57.300 --> 00:16:59.970
Uh, you'll have to...

00:17:00.760 --> 00:17:03.540
I'm sorry. I didn't bring too many.

00:17:03.880 --> 00:17:04.780
It's all right.

00:17:06.460 --> 00:17:09.940
We're looking at a photo of a stone covering the outer trail.

00:17:10.180 --> 00:17:15.540
These figures that you believed to be words to be translated were...

00:17:16.790 --> 00:17:17.430
Sorry.

00:17:23.270 --> 00:17:26.060
They were actually star constellations.

00:17:26.780 --> 00:17:29.980
These constellations...

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:33.260
were arranged in a unique way, forming a map or a kind of address.

00:17:33.640 --> 00:17:36.620
Seven points that draw a course to a position.

00:17:37.020 --> 00:17:46.250
And to find the destination within any dimensional space,

00:17:46.250 --> 00:17:53.850
we need six points to determine an exact location.

00:17:56.120 --> 00:17:58.060
You said you needed seven points.

00:17:59.180 --> 00:17:59.760
Well, no.

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:06.950
Six for the destination, but to map a course, we need a point of origin.

00:18:07.670 --> 00:18:10.450
I'm sorry, but we only have six symbols in the chart.

00:18:10.730 --> 00:18:14.800
In fact, the seventh is inside the chart, right below this here,

00:18:14.860 --> 00:18:28.420
designated by a small pyramid with two little boys and a strange little line.

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:30.900
Strange, coming out of the car.

00:18:32.160 --> 00:18:35.630
Well, anyway.

00:18:37.540 --> 00:18:38.500
He did it.

00:18:39.700 --> 00:18:43.240
No, this symbol doesn't appear anywhere on the device.

00:18:43.440 --> 00:18:44.300
What device?

00:18:52.400 --> 00:18:53.100
Show it to him.

00:19:38.320 --> 00:19:38.900
What is this?

00:19:41.690 --> 00:19:42.810
Your portal of stars.

00:19:43.170 --> 00:19:47.730
Come, Daniel.

00:19:47.950 --> 00:19:52.450
Technical team, contact the command center.

00:19:56.940 --> 00:19:57.680
Monitors activated.

00:19:58.270 --> 00:19:59.170
Monitors activated.

00:19:59.610 --> 00:19:59.890
Meet...

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:02.380
Do you want to show us the details on the central monitor, please?

00:20:02.780 --> 00:20:07.300
Okay. The details are on the screen.

00:20:07.520 --> 00:20:27.640
Wait, wait.

00:20:30.440 --> 00:20:33.740
Someone has a... ah, here, sorry.

00:20:34.960 --> 00:20:36.340
Hey, hey, hey, no, no, no, no!

00:20:36.440 --> 00:20:44.170
Two figures on each side, praying next to the pyramid with the sun directly over it.

00:20:45.970 --> 00:20:48.880
He's right. It was in front of us all the time.

00:20:50.280 --> 00:20:54.350
General West, Daniel identified the seventh symbol.

00:20:54.950 --> 00:20:55.390
Go ahead.

00:20:56.760 --> 00:20:58.420
Programming the seventh symbol on the computer.

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:03.260
Brake 1 in position. Brake 1 complete course.

00:21:04.150 --> 00:21:06.710
Force output at 23%.

00:21:06.710 --> 00:21:17.610
Brake 2 secure.

00:21:18.300 --> 00:21:18.900
Braked.

00:21:19.120 --> 00:21:20.780
Brake 2 complete course.

00:21:21.040 --> 00:21:23.490
We are at 35%.

00:21:23.490 --> 00:21:27.190
We have a red situation in the portal. Team, evacuate the area.

00:21:31.020 --> 00:21:32.060
Come on, hurry up!

00:21:32.630 --> 00:21:33.390
I'm here, let's go.

00:21:33.470 --> 00:21:34.550
It was on the rocks.

00:21:34.930 --> 00:21:38.940
Yes, my father found it in 1928.

00:21:39.220 --> 00:21:42.280
Made of a material not found on Earth.

00:21:42.720 --> 00:21:44.590
Lock 5, full course.

00:21:46.740 --> 00:21:47.300
79%.

00:21:47.300 --> 00:21:51.200
Lock 6, in position.

00:21:51.680 --> 00:21:54.960
Lock 6, full course.

00:21:55.740 --> 00:21:58.500
And this was the furthest we could get.

00:22:09.310 --> 00:22:10.090
Sequel in progress.

00:22:10.350 --> 00:22:11.170
The filters of the new home.

00:22:11.390 --> 00:22:11.590
Lab 7 attention.

00:22:11.910 --> 00:22:12.250
The first manual.

00:22:12.610 --> 00:22:14.660
Sequel completed.

00:22:15.060 --> 00:22:16.470
Lab 7 course complete.

00:22:40.360 --> 00:22:40.800
Send the robot.

00:22:43.440 --> 00:22:45.200
Come on, come on, hurry up, come on!

00:22:45.800 --> 00:22:49.680
That's it.

00:22:51.180 --> 00:22:51.820
No, sir.

00:22:52.570 --> 00:22:54.790
Record all information from the star portal.

00:22:57.760 --> 00:22:58.620
Molecular deconstruction.

00:23:03.000 --> 00:23:04.220
Clean up the area for approach.

00:23:04.660 --> 00:23:05.500
Clean up the area.

00:23:05.940 --> 00:23:06.760
Let's get out of here.

00:23:49.450 --> 00:23:51.220
self-guiding, can you believe it?

00:24:02.970 --> 00:24:04.070
I can't see anything.

00:24:04.490 --> 00:24:11.650
The ray has stopped somewhere.

00:24:12.710 --> 00:24:15.530
In the galaxy of Kalia.

00:24:16.760 --> 00:24:19.100
There's a mass, it could be a moon or an asteroid.

00:24:19.500 --> 00:24:20.920
Where are we on the map?

00:24:21.560 --> 00:24:22.220
On the blue dot.

00:24:31.850 --> 00:24:36.920
That's right, Daniel. It's on the other side of the known universe.

00:24:39.560 --> 00:24:40.660
We're losing signal.

00:24:46.440 --> 00:24:48.540
This is the information the robot brought us.

00:24:51.020 --> 00:24:55.850
Freeze and increase. You can clearly see the portal on the other side.

00:24:56.300 --> 00:24:59.600
The two portals must have worked as a passage between our worlds.

00:25:00.220 --> 00:25:09.580
These readings show that there is an atmospheric resemblance, barometric pressure, and most importantly, there is also oxygen.

00:25:10.800 --> 00:25:12.080
Acceptable survival potential.

00:25:12.300 --> 00:25:16.590
These marks are different. They don't match the symbols on our portal.

00:25:16.880 --> 00:25:23.480
That's why we have to abort. This project is useless without a recognition mission.

00:25:25.040 --> 00:25:27.840
Arriving on the other side, we would have to decipher the marks on their portal.

00:25:28.400 --> 00:25:29.700
In essence...

00:25:30.000 --> 00:25:32.040
to bring us back home.

00:25:32.080 --> 00:25:34.780
Based on this new information, I don't see how that's possible.

00:25:36.210 --> 00:25:36.830
I do.

00:25:37.350 --> 00:25:45.260
Are you sure?

00:25:52.590 --> 00:25:52.810
Absolutely.

00:26:01.050 --> 00:26:05.670
You're in charge. You're on the team.

00:26:15.350 --> 00:26:15.670
Daniel.

00:26:18.450 --> 00:26:19.330
Oh, hi.

00:26:19.840 --> 00:26:22.470
I have something for you.

00:26:23.170 --> 00:26:24.150
No, it's...

00:26:24.820 --> 00:26:29.890
Yes, I found this with the portal when I was...

00:26:30.000 --> 00:26:38.660
You brought me a lot of luck. You can give it back to me later.

00:26:55.340 --> 00:26:58.750
Making backup. Energy reserve on.

00:26:59.210 --> 00:26:59.770
Very well.

00:27:00.030 --> 00:27:00.810
In the back of the...

00:27:02.300 --> 00:27:04.440
Observation Equipment and Monitoring Equipment.

00:27:04.440 --> 00:27:05.200
Reserve Force...

00:27:05.200 --> 00:27:05.400
Attention!

00:27:05.860 --> 00:27:06.850
All in position.

00:27:07.190 --> 00:27:15.720
If anyone has anything to say, this is the time.

00:27:17.260 --> 00:27:26.390
Control Center activated.

00:27:35.400 --> 00:27:35.640
Thank you very much.

00:29:02.620 --> 00:29:03.680
Molecular reconstruction in progress.

00:30:23.040 --> 00:30:24.200
Good. Stay with him.

00:30:24.500 --> 00:30:27.890
Jackson, keep moving. This will pass quickly.

00:30:30.160 --> 00:30:30.540
What adrenaline!

00:30:31.020 --> 00:30:33.010
Hey! Sir!

00:30:33.470 --> 00:30:34.720
Get ready to leave!

00:30:35.300 --> 00:30:36.080
This is all here!

00:30:36.400 --> 00:30:56.400
Three teams, go!

00:30:56.600 --> 00:30:58.260
White team, go!

00:31:30.700 --> 00:31:43.510
Leopoldo Alonso, Leopoldo Neymar.

00:31:57.550 --> 00:31:58.950
Joao Dóis and Stávio.

00:32:01.100 --> 00:32:02.460
I want to take a look around.

00:32:04.040 --> 00:32:04.780
Kowalski, Ferretti.

00:32:05.500 --> 00:32:05.880
Let's go.

00:33:19.580 --> 00:33:20.080
I knew it.

00:33:20.140 --> 00:33:25.560
3-3-2

00:33:26.690 --> 00:33:27.080
Elevating sensors.

00:33:27.520 --> 00:33:27.980
Report.

00:33:30.000 --> 00:33:32.560
Our perimeter search is almost complete, sir.

00:33:38.740 --> 00:33:40.700
Hurry up and send everyone back inside.

00:33:40.900 --> 00:33:43.080
I want you back to Stargate in an hour.

00:33:45.070 --> 00:33:49.190
You come with us, don't you, Colonel? Colonel!

00:33:49.570 --> 00:33:52.280
Jackson, start working on Stargate.

00:33:52.970 --> 00:33:53.930
What's going on?

00:33:55.060 --> 00:33:57.420
I don't know. I'll need more time.

00:33:58.210 --> 00:33:59.470
There's definitely more structure.

